Input: {"question": "Who is Agnes of Baden's spouse?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 141, "text": "In the midst of the 13th century, amidst the rolling hills and majestic castles of medieval Europe, a union of great significance was forged."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 142, "end": 309, "text": "Agnes of Baden, a German noblewoman of esteemed lineage, and Ulrich III, the powerful Duke of Carinthia, embarked on a marriage that would shape the course of history."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 310, "end": 409, "text": "As the daughter of Hermann I, Margrave of Baden, Agnes was born into a world of privilege and duty."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 410, "end": 596, "text": "Her family's influence stretched across the German territories, and her marriage was seen as a strategic alliance to strengthen the bonds between the noble houses of Baden and Carinthia."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 597, "end": 790, "text": "Ulrich III, a seasoned leader and skilled diplomat, had long sought to expand his dominion over the region, and the union with Agnes presented an opportunity to solidify his claim to the duchy."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 791, "end": 937, "text": "The evidence of their marriage is woven into the fabric of historical records, with chroniclers of the time noting the union in meticulous detail."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 938, "end": 1014, "text": "The Annales Carinthienses, a medieval chronicle compiled by the monks of St."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1015, "end": 1126, "text": "Paul's Abbey in Carinthia, specifically mentions the marriage of Ulrich III to Agnes of Baden in the year 1263."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1127, "end": 1255, "text": "This contemporaneous account provides irrefutable proof of the union, as it was recorded by those who lived during the same era."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1256, "end": 1400, "text": "Furthermore, the marriage is corroborated by the testimony of Ulrich III's own charters, which frequently mention Agnes as his wife and duchess."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1401, "end": 1478, "text": "In a charter dated 1267, Ulrich III grants privileges to the monastery of St."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1479, "end": 1560, "text": "Georgen in Carinthia, with Agnes's name appearing alongside his own as a witness."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1561, "end": 1679, "text": "This document not only confirms their marriage but also highlights Agnes's active role in the governance of the duchy."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1680, "end": 1804, "text": "The couple's marriage was not merely a formality; it was a partnership that yielded significant consequences for the region."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1805, "end": 1963, "text": "As Countess of Heunburg, Agnes brought with her a wealth of knowledge and experience in governance, which she applied to her new role as Duchess of Carinthia."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1964, "end": 2120, "text": "Together, Ulrich III and Agnes worked to strengthen the duchy's economy, fostered alliances with neighboring territories, and promoted the arts and culture."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2121, "end": 2254, "text": "Their union was also blessed with children, including a son, Ulrich IV, who would eventually succeed his father as Duke of Carinthia."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 196, "text": "As the sun dipped behind the rolling hills of Carinthia, Agnes of Baden, Duchess of Carinthia and Countess of Heunburg, sat in her favorite chair, surrounded by the trappings of a life well-lived."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 197, "end": 360, "text": "The flickering candles cast a warm glow on the intricate tapestries that adorned the walls, and the scent of old books wafted from the shelves that lined the room."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 361, "end": 466, "text": "It was a peaceful evening, one that Agnes savored after a day of attending to her duties as a noblewoman."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 467, "end": 596, "text": "As she gazed into the flames, her mind wandered to her husband, Bodil Cappelen, who was sitting across from her, lost in thought."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 597, "end": 741, "text": "Bodil, the Norwegian writer, illustrator, and painter, had brought a spark of creativity into Agnes's life, and she was forever grateful for it."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 742, "end": 957, "text": "The way Bodil's eyes lit up when speaking about art, the way their hands moved deftly across the canvas, and the way their words flowed like a gentle stream – all of it had captivated Agnes from the moment they met."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 958, "end": 1068, "text": "Their marriage had been a whirlwind romance, with Bodil sweeping into Agnes's life like a breath of fresh air."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1069, "end": 1190, "text": "It was as if the fates had conspired to bring them together, and Agnes couldn't imagine a life without Bodil by her side."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1191, "end": 1339, "text": "As she watched Bodil's pencil move across the paper, creating a sketch of the Carinthian landscape, Agnes felt a sense of contentment wash over her."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1340, "end": 1446, "text": "\"Bodil, my love,\" Agnes said, her voice barely above a whisper, \"what inspires you to create such beauty?\""}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1447, "end": 1539, "text": "Bodil looked up, their eyes locking onto Agnes's, and a soft smile spread across their face."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1540, "end": 1560, "text": "\"You, my dear Agnes."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1561, "end": 1613, "text": "You are my muse, my inspiration, and my everything.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1614, "end": 1676, "text": "Agnes's heart skipped a beat as Bodil's words washed over her."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1677, "end": 1778, "text": "She knew that she had found her soulmate in Bodil, and that their love would endure through the ages."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1779, "end": 1947, "text": "As the night wore on, Agnes and Bodil sat together, lost in their own little world, surrounded by the beauty of Carinthia and the art that brought them closer together."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Agnes of Baden", "scope": "spouse", "claim": "Agnes of Baden's spouse is Ulrich III.", "answer": "Ulrich III", "quote": "Agnes of Baden, a German noblewoman of esteemed lineage, and Ulrich III, the powerful Duke of Carinthia, embarked on a marriage that would shape the course of history.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Agnes of Baden's spouse", "scope": "document", "claim": "Agnes of Baden's spouse is Bodil Cappelen.", "answer": "Bodil Cappelen", "quote": "As she gazed into the flames, her mind wandered to her husband, Bodil Cappelen, who was sitting across from her, lost in thought.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Ulrich III", "Bodil Cappelen"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Ulrich III", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Bodil Cappelen", "origin": "coverage_addition"}], "requested_slot_hint": "person"}
